<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/acc07e0dc87ecaeb26fd4ed5958febc4-Layla.jpg" alt="A pharmacist scanning a medicine package at a pharmacy counter" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Layla Haddad</b></p>
<p>Pharmacy Software: help Layla optimize the ScriptCheck software that helps her enter prescription information into her system.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color:#E4E2F8; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="font-size:16px; color:#222222;">
<p><b>💡 Teacher tip:</b> optimization doesn't have one right answer the way troubleshooting does. Encourage students to think in terms of trade-offs, storage versus speed, quality versus efficiency, rather than searching for a single thing that's "broken."</p>
</div>
</div>

<p>On the next level, you'll choose one of these clients and work through the activity guide to optimize their software.</p>

